######## ATTADIPA PEDOMETER PROBE ########
Writes CTRL2/CTRL7/CTRL8 on the IMU at 0x6B. Nothing else, on any
device. No PMU write, no rail change, no display.

WHO_AM_I  = 0x05   (0x05 in both candidate datasheets)
REVISION  = 0x7C   (0x7C = QMI8658A 13-52-25 Rev A; 0x79 = QMI8658C Rev 0.6)

--- before ---   CTRL2=0x24 CTRL7=0x03 CTRL8=0x00
writing CTRL2 = 0x26  (+/-8 g, 125 Hz accel-only)  -> ACK
writing CTRL7 = 0x01  (aEN)                        -> ACK
writing CTRL8 = 0x90  (Pedo_EN + STATUSINT handshake) -> ACK
--- after  ---   CTRL2=0x26 CTRL7=0x01 CTRL8=0x90

CTRL8 readback: accepted -- the register is writable, which the C Rev 0.6
  document does not describe (it calls CTRL8 Reserved: Not Used)

Accelerometer and step count, once a second. +/-8 g full scale means
4096 LSB/g, so a board lying still should show ~4096 on one axis.
Pick the watch up and walk with it to move the step counter.

